\label{def:fixed-coordinate}
Fixed-coordinate recovery freezes $W_{2,i}$ and $W_{1,i}$ and adapts only an
internal middle map
$C_i=I_{k_i}+A_iB_i$, where
$A_i\in\mathbb R^{k_i\times r_a}$,
$B_i\in\mathbb R^{r_a\times k_i}$, and $r_a\ll k_i$.
The recovered operator is
\begin{equation}
\widetilde W_i
=
W_{2,i}C_iW_{1,i}
=
W_{2,i}(I_{k_i}+A_iB_i)W_{1,i}.
\label{eq:fixed-coordinate}
\end{equation}
